  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Original 609 whole living lungfish. Two clearly separate dorsal fins and blunt tooth-plate-bearing head. No slab, detached jaw, or fin-only substitution. [\"Living body cross-section, skin color and soft lip margins speculative.\", \"Source fossils are laterally compressed, dorsal/ventral fin overlap can conceal paired fins. Use bilateral paired fins, not all fins on one side.\", \"Tooth plate cusp count is simplified, not exact histological reconstruction; tiny structures may be proportionally clarified without detached oversized props.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"total_length_m\": 0.2, \"status\": \"Approximate specimen-informed artistic scale: Achanarras IMG_6882a has 2 cm bar about110px versus fish about1100px (~20cm); not a published precise measurement. PLOS Fig9 has10mm bar.\", \"body_width_m\": 0.035, \"body_height_m\": 0.047, \"uncertainty\": \"Body thickness and living soft tissues reconstructed, not measured from compressed specimen; do not describe20cm as species maximum.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：Original 609 whole living lungfish. Two clearly separate dorsal fins and blunt tooth-plate-bearing head. No slab, detached jaw, or fin-only substitution. [\"Living body cross-section, skin color and soft lip margins speculative.\", \"Source fossils are laterally compressed, dorsal/ventral fin overlap can conceal paired fins. Use bilateral paired fins, not all fins on one side.\", \"Tooth plate cusp count is simplified, not exact histological reconstruction; tiny structures may be proportionally clarified without detached oversized props.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"total_length_m\": 0.2, \"status\": \"Approximate specimen-informed artistic scale: Achanarras IMG_6882a has 2 cm bar about110px versus fish about1100px (~20cm); not a published precise measurement. PLOS Fig9 has10mm bar.\", \"body_width_m\": 0.035, \"body_height_m\": 0.047, \"uncertainty\": \"Body thickness and living soft tissues reconstructed, not measured from compressed specimen; do not describe20cm as species maximum.\"}"
  },
